---
description: Commits, docs, and GitHub Releases use the real clock — never frozen GIT_*_DATE
alwaysApply: true
---

# Real git timestamps

Never `export GIT_AUTHOR_DATE` or `GIT_COMMITTER_DATE`. Do not copy those values from an older commit when rewriting (`commit-tree`, amend, strip trailers). If they are already in the environment, `unset GIT_AUTHOR_DATE GIT_COMMITTER_DATE` before any `git commit`. Rewrite Cursor trailers in a **subshell** so those variables do not leak.

GitHub lists files by **author date**. A frozen stamp makes every touched file look hours old even when the merge is new.

`CHANGES.md` dates and docs **Last Updated** are today's date.

CI must not set `SOURCE_DATE_EPOCH` on the Release job. `make test` fails if `GIT_AUTHOR_DATE` or `GIT_COMMITTER_DATE` is set.

Branding (no Cursor co-author): `.cursor/rules/branding.mdc`.
